# Resource costs — image + number

## Hard rule
Whenever UI shows a **resource amount being spent, held, rewarded, or priced**, render it as **icon image + number**. Do not use text-only labels like `−골드 150` or `크리스탈 8` as the primary cost display.

## Approved pattern
```html
<span class="res-cost-chip">
  <img class="res-ico" src="/art/ui/res/gold.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" draggable="false" />
  <strong>150</strong>
</span>
```

Prefer shared helpers (`resCostChip`, `shopPriceMana`, `shopPriceCrystal`, mission reward chips) over one-off markup.

## Asset map (common)
| Resource | Path |
|----------|------|
| Gold | `/art/ui/res/gold.svg` |
| Crystal | `/art/ui/res/crystal.svg` |
| Energy | `/art/ui/res/energy.svg` |
| Grindstone | `/art/ui/res/grindstone.webp` |
| Imprint stone | `/art/ui/res/imprint-stone.webp` |
| Jinmun | `/art/ui/res/jinmun.svg` |
| Skill mat | `/art/ui/res/skill-mat.svg` |

## Disallowed
```ts
cost: `${MINUS}${t("ui.gold")} ${n}` // text-only primary cost
```
```html
<p>−연마석 1 · −골드 150</p> <!-- no icons -->
```

## Checklist
1. Cost / reward / stock chips use `<img>` + numeric amount.
2. Multiple costs = multiple chips side by side (not a prose sentence).
3. Confirm / forge / shop / mission UIs follow the same pattern.
4. Accessible name can stay on `title` / parent label; the visible cost is still image + number.
